      "intro": "If your loved one struggles with heating bills, LIHEAP can provide $25–750 toward their heating costs each year, plus up to $600 in emergency assistance when utility shutoff threatens. Because this is income-based assistance (not age-restricted), any household earning less than $2,608/month for one person qualifies, and if your loved one already gets SNAP or cash assistance, they're automatically eligible.\n\nMaryland runs LIHEAP through three connected programs: MEAP for heating assistance, EUSP for electric bill grants, and year-round crisis help. Because payments go directly to the utility company, your loved one never handles the money, the assistance appears as a credit on their bill. The catch: funding is limited and applications close when money runs out, so apply early in the program year.",
