      "intro": "If your loved one lives alone in Maryland, the Senior Call Check Program provides daily automated wellness calls at a time they choose between 8 a.m. and 4 p.m. When your loved one doesn't answer after three attempts, the program calls you or another contact person to encourage a welfare check.\n\nBecause the program operates every day except six holidays, your loved one gets consistent daily contact even when family schedules are busy. If both your loved one and the alternate contact can't be reached, local non-emergency law enforcement conducts a welfare check.\n\nThe program is completely free with no income or asset limits, your loved one just needs to be 60 or older and live in Maryland with access to a phone.",
